arguments.prompt:
You are working in /tmp/sv-22a416f3b7c447a6903e3ca405a85260/ShipmentTracker which is a Blazor Web App with Interactive Auto Global mode and Individual authentication.

The project structure:
- ShipmentTracker/ (server project) - has EF Core with SQLite, ASP.NET Core Identity
- ShipmentTracker.Client/ (client project) - interactive components go here

The app is for a logistics company tracking shipments. Implement these features:

## 1. Remove template pages
Delete these files:
- ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Counter.razor
- ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Weather.razor

## 2. Create shared model in Client project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Status { get; set; } = "Pending";
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; } = DateTime.UtcNow;
}
```

## 3. Create service interface in Client project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
    Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, string status);
}
```
Make sure to add the using for Models.

## 4. Create Client-side HttpClient implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>())!;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, string status)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", new { Status = status });
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>())!;
    }
}
```

## 5. Register HttpClient and service in Client Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to add:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => sp.GetRequiredService<IHttpClientFactory>().CreateClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI"));
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

## 6. Add Shipment entity to server's DbContext

The server already has `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`. Edit it to add:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
```
And add a DbSet property:
```csharp
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```

## 7. Create server-side service implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.CreatedAt).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        shipment.TrackingNumber = $"SHP-{Guid.NewGuid().ToString()[..8].ToUpper()}";
        shipment.CreatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow;
        db.Shipments.Add(shipment);
        await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, string status)
    {
        var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id) ?? throw new InvalidOperationException("Shipment not found");
        shipment.Status = status;
        await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }
}
```

## 8. Add API endpoints and register server service in server Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`. After the line `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEmailSender<ApplicationUser>, IdentityNoOpEmailSender>();`, add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServerService>();
```

Add necessary usings at the top:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
```

Before `app.Run();`, add the API endpoints:
```csharp
// Shipment API endpoints
var shipments = app.MapGroup("api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

shipments.MapGet("/", async (IShipmentService service) =>
    Results.Ok(await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync()));

shipments.MapGet("/track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
{
    var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
    return shipment is not null ? Results.Ok(shipment) : Results.NotFound();
}).AllowAnonymous();

shipments.MapPost("/", async (Shipment shipment, IShipmentService service) =>
{
    var created = await service.CreateShipmentAsync(shipment);
    return Results.Created($"api/shipments/{created.Id}", created);
});

shipments.MapPut("/{id}/status", async (int id, StatusUpdate update, IShipmentService service) =>
{
    var updated = await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, update.Status);
    return Results.Ok(updated);
});
```

Also add a record for the status update DTO right before `app.Run();` or as a top-level type. Actually, put it after the endpoints and before `app.Run();` as a file-scoped type won't work there. Instead, define a minimal record at the bottom of the file after `app.Run();`:
```csharp
public record StatusUpdate(string Status);
```

## 9. Create the pages in the Client project

### Home.razor - Replace existing with landing page:
Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor`:
```razor
@page "/"

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
